::ingredients

(broccoli, fresh preferred or frozen) 1-2
(garlic, minced) 1tbsp
(ginger, minced) 1tbsp
(wine choice) = (sherry) 1tbsp -OR- (white wine) 1tbsp
(soy sauce) 1-2tbsp
# Method-only ingredients
(oil, sesame seed or neutral or olive) 1tsp
(water, steaming) ~1/2in / 1.57cm depth as stated
(liquid choice) = (water, warm) 1/2 cup / ~120ml -OR- (chicken stock) 1/2 cup / ~120ml
(sugar; brown) to taste
(lemon juice) to taste
(cornstarch) as needed to thicken

::equipment

(knife, paring)
(pan) -OR- (wok)
(lid)

::instructions

(broccoli) <cut, little florets, upside down and cut around stem with paring knife>
(water, steaming) <pour, pan or wok, ~1/2in / 1.57cm as source states>
    <bring to boil, rapidly>
(broccoli) <steam, lid on, ~3m>
    <drain>
(pan) <wipe, dry>
(oil) + (garlic) + (ginger) <sauté>
    + (wine choice) <deglaze>
{sauce} = (oil) + (garlic) + (ginger) + (wine choice) + (liquid choice)
{sauce} <reduce, medium-high>
    + (soy sauce) + (sugar) + (lemon juice) <stir, to taste>
    + (cornstarch) <thicken>
(broccoli) + {sauce} <sauté, very briefly, retain crunch>

::story

Asian inspired broccoli dish with tasty sauce. Sauce can be used for all kinds of Asian inspired sauted vegetables.

